  "query_preview": "..\n\nHigh pressure centered over northern lower MI has maintained a \npleasant fall day across SE MI. East-northeast winds have wrapped \nenough lake moisture around the periphery of core subsidence to \nsupport a healthy coverage of diurnal cumulus over the \nsouthern/eastern portions of the area with sunny skies holding over \nthe western/northern portions. Clouds fade early this evening with \nsunset leading to another cool night with lows falling into the \nlower 40s. \n\nA shortwave trough currently working across the upper Midwest tracks \ninto the north-central Great Lakes late tonight as high pressure is \nshunted east. Moisture transport isn't particularly strong due to \nweak lower level winds (sub 40kts below 700mb), however is enough to \ndraw in ribbon of modest theta-e from the Midwest along the lead \nedge of the mid-level wave/PV anomaly. Isentropic ascent is also \nconfined along this lead edge resulting in a narrow band of \npotential showers sliding across between ~09-13Z. Owing to closer \nproximity to the shortwave and cold pool, said shower chances \nessentially confined north of I-69. Surface cold front lags, not \ncrossing until Sunday evening, with minimal fanfare outside a low \nchance for an isolated shower/drizzle. \n\nSome of the coolest air of the season thus far follows as 850mb \ntemps fall to 1-2C by Sunday night dropping lows to the low 40s-\nupper 30s. Thermal troughing holds over the central Great Lakes \nthrough Monday as 850mb temps nudge down further to around 0C \nlimiting diurnal recovery to highs near 60. Building surface high \npressure late day Monday promotes clearing skies and near calm winds \nby Monday night supporting SE MI's first shot at frost, particularly \nacross the Saginaw Valley/Thumb, as lows approach the mid 30s. More \nseasonably average temperatures return for the midweek period as \nHudson Bay upper troughing shifts towards Labrador.",
